WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.842
AI agents are starting to do the buying.

00:00:02.872 --> 00:00:05.031
But the webshop was built for people.

00:00:05.061 --> 00:00:07.325
So who signs for the machine?

00:00:08.033 --> 00:00:09.838
This is AimoPilot.

00:00:09.868 --> 00:00:12.984
Let AI do the buying, and keep the last word.

00:00:13.014 --> 00:00:16.805
Built for Valio Aimo, at Junction 2026.

00:00:17.633 --> 00:00:21.810
A kitchen asks for a thousand litres of lactose-free milk by Monday.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:26.227
The agent searches seventeen thousand products, and prices just three.

00:00:26.257 --> 00:00:30.701
The usual boxes can't make Monday, so it offers three ranked options.

00:00:30.731 --> 00:00:33.897
It's over the limit, so a person signs on their phone.

00:00:33.927 --> 00:00:36.803
One passkey, and it's placed at a fixed price.

00:00:36.833 --> 00:00:38.548
The model is never trusted.

00:00:38.578 --> 00:00:41.770
Twenty rules in plain code check every order.

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:46.530
We tried a forged mandate, a replayed quote, an agent approving itself.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:50.133
All stopped, and all on a tamper-evident ledger.

00:00:50.433 --> 00:00:54.589
Six agents, built on the AI SDK and MCP:

00:00:54.619 --> 00:01:03.947
the buyer, by text or voice, a menu planner, a stock-out watch, the wholesaler's seller, any outside agent, and an operations copilot.

00:01:03.977 --> 00:01:06.095
None can order past the gate.

00:01:06.333 --> 00:01:08.728
It remembers how each kitchen buys.

00:01:08.758 --> 00:01:14.511
So it catches four thousand litres instead of four hundred, and asks only when it matters.

00:01:15.233 --> 00:01:20.019
Vector and keyword search recall fifty candidates, inside the kitchen's rules.

00:01:20.049 --> 00:01:23.405
A decision model judges them, and code checks the judge.

00:01:23.435 --> 00:01:27.410
Standard search is right first time seventy-two percent at best.

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:28.450
AimoPilot?

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:29.603
Ninety-seven.

00:01:29.633 --> 00:01:31.288
All of it runs on Aiven:

00:01:31.318 --> 00:01:43.331
Runtime hosts the app, Postgres holds the ledger and memory, Kafka carries every action, Valkey caches live prices, OpenSearch runs keyword and vector search, and Grafana watches it all.

00:01:43.361 --> 00:01:49.103
A Managed Agent buys through our MCP door, and Aiven's MCP server feeds our copilot.

00:01:49.133 --> 00:01:54.056
The wholesaler sees every agent and every decision, and can stop any of them.

00:01:54.086 --> 00:01:55.090
AimoPilot.

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:56.948
Keep the last word.

